      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Debug & visualization toolbox\n\nNone of the data nodes in this pack draw anything (visualization is always a SEPARATE node) - so this sheet collects the inspection and rendering nodes you reach for while building a pipeline. Most are flagged 'Debug helper' in their description. There are two domains:\n\nNPARRAY domain (raw cv2 arrays) - 'Preview CV Array' renders any 2-D/3-D array three ways (image = values as-is; normalize = min-max stretch for gradients/distance/score maps; heatmap = normalize + viridis), with an optional labelled value bar. 'Inspect CV Data' prints shape/dtype/min/max/mean of ANYTHING (its on-node text does not render, so it is paired with core 'Preview as Text'). 'CV Array Statistic' reduces a field to one value per channel and a readable string. 'Flow To Color' renders a vector/angle field as the optical-flow colour wheel. The Draw* nodes (Text, Contours, Points, Polygon) stamp overlays onto a copy and chain - here they stack on one image. Because they share that image they also differ by SHAPE and LINE STYLE, not only by colour: crosses for the points, a dashed quad, solid contours. Colour alone is the one channel a colour-blind viewer may not have, and it is the first thing lost in greyscale. 'Stack Images' tiles before/after comparisons.\n\nIMAGE domain (curated nodes) - 'CV Color Map' false-colours a grayscale IMAGE (depth/heat/mask) with a colour bar; 'CV Overlay Masks' tints each connected component a different colour over the photo. Both output IMAGE, shown with core 'Preview Image'.\n\nMore draw nodes live in dedicated playgrounds: Draw Segments/Circles (18 Hough), Draw Flow Grid (22 optical flow), Draw Keypoints/Matches/Epilines (the homography/epipolar exercises)."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
